// An UN-ANNOTATED parameter whose body's returns join to a value union. `vl check` returns 0
// and the emitter refuses with `emitProgram: narrowed union atom has no value box`. Annotate
// the parameter — `function pick(b: boolean)` — and the identical body RUNS and prints 1, so
// the union rep is not missing; only the un-annotated route to it is.
//
// FOUND 2026-09-01 while auditing which refusals `goal-scoreboard.py` counts. Its CONCEDES
// filter matches phrasings that ADMIT a capability gap, and this message does not use one —
// so a reachable clause-2 violation was invisible to the number. See D964: the filter is a
// LOWER BOUND, not the population.
// Should print 1.
function pick(b) {
  if b { return 1 }
  "s"
}

print(pick(true))
